IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa15-nouns`
IMPORT `coa15-ch1`

-- coa15-ch3.l4: Part 18, Chapter 3 (Redeemable shares), ss 684 to 689 (lines 9030-9080 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat. It imports coa15-ch1.l4 for the statement-of-capital check of s 663(3) (the
-- same five words recur in s 689(3)). Reading a result: as in coa15-ch1.l4.

DECLARE `s 685(3) act in Chapter 3` IS ONE OF
    `s 685(3)(a) determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of the shares`
    `s 686(3) pay for the shares on redemption`
    `s 689(1) give notice to the registrar of the redemption, specifying the shares redeemed`

-- ---- s 684: power of a limited company to issue redeemable shares ----------------------------------------

-- src:9032 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may issue shares that are to be redeemed or are liable to be redeemed at the option of the company or the shareholder (“redeemable shares”), subject to the following provisions.
@ref s 684(1) A limited company having a share capital may issue redeemable shares (src:9032-9032)
GIVEN `the shares are to be redeemed or are liable to be redeemed at the option of the company or the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 684(1) the shares are redeemable shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are to be redeemed or are liable to be redeemed at the option of the company or the shareholder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares that are to be redeemed or are liable to be redeemed at the option of the company or the shareholder (“redeemable shares”)"

@ref s 684(1) A limited company having a share capital may issue redeemable shares (src:9032-9032)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 684(1) the company may issue redeemable shares` MEANS
    IF `the company is a limited company having a share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A limited company having a share capital may issue shares that are to be redeemed"

-- src:9033 | (2) The articles of a private limited company may exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares.
@ref s 684(2) The articles of a private limited company may exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares (src:9033-9033)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 684(2) the articles may exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private limited company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The articles of a private limited company may exclude or restrict the issue of redeemable shares"

-- src:9034 | (3) A public limited company may only issue redeemable shares if it is authorised to do so by its articles.
@ref s 684(3) A public limited company may only issue redeemable shares if it is authorised to do so by its articles (src:9034-9034)
GIVEN `the company is a public limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is authorised to issue redeemable shares by its articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 684(3) the public limited company may issue redeemable shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public limited company may only issue redeemable shares"
    ELSE IF `the company is authorised to issue redeemable shares by its articles`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only issue redeemable shares if it is authorised to do so by its articles"

-- src:9035 | (4) No redeemable shares may be issued at a time when there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable.
@ref s 684(4) No redeemable shares may be issued at a time when there are no issued shares that are not redeemable (src:9035-9035)
GIVEN `there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 684(4) the issue of redeemable shares is barred` MEANS
    IF `there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No redeemable shares may be issued at a time when there are no issued shares of the company that are not redeemable"

-- ---- s 685: terms and manner of redemption ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9037 | (1) The directors of a limited company may determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of shares if they are authorised to do so—
-- src:9038 | (a) by the company's articles, or
-- src:9039 | (b) by a resolution of the company.
@ref s 685(1) The directors may determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption if authorised by the articles or by a resolution (src:9037-9039)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are authorised by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 685(1) the directors may determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-685-1: "the directors may determine the terms" ("if they are authorised") is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    IF (NOT `the company is a limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of a limited company may determine"
    ELSE IF `the directors are authorised by the company's articles` OR `the directors are authorised by a resolution of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if they are authorised to do so— (a) by the company's articles, or (b) by a resolution of the company"

-- src:9040 | (2) A resolution under subsection (1)(b) may be an ordinary resolution, even though it amends the company's articles.
@ref s 685(2) A resolution under subsection (1)(b) may be an ordinary resolution, even though it amends the company's articles (src:9040-9040)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 685(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 685(2) the resolution is a good resolution under subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 685(1)(b)`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- an ordinary resolution suffices "even though it amends the company's articles"
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be an ordinary resolution": the text says an ordinary resolution may do; it does not say that another kind may not
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution under subsection (1)(b)"

-- src:9041 | (3) Where the directors are authorised under subsection (1) to determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of shares—
-- src:9042 | (a) they must do so before the shares are allotted, and
@ref s 685(3)(a) Where the directors are authorised, they must determine the terms before the shares are allotted (src:9041-9042)
GIVEN `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the directors determined the terms, conditions and manner of redemption` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the shares are allotted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 685(3)(a) the directors determined the terms before the shares were allotted` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors are authorised under subsection (1) to determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of shares"
    ELSE IF `the date on which the directors determined the terms, conditions and manner of redemption` LESS THAN `the date on which the shares are allotted`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they must do so before the shares are allotted"

@ref s 685(3)(a) Where the directors are authorised, they must determine the terms before the shares are allotted (src:9041-9042)
GIVEN `the date on which the directors begin` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the shares are allotted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 685(3) act in Chapter 3`
`s 685(3)(a) the directors must determine the terms before the shares are allotted` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 685(3)(a) determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of the shares`
    WITHIN (Day `the date on which the shares are allotted` MINUS Day `the date on which the directors begin` MINUS 1)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 685(3)(a): the terms of redemption were not determined before the shares were allotted"

-- src:9041 | (3) Where the directors are authorised under subsection (1) to determine the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of shares—
-- src:9042 | (a) they must do so before the shares are allotted, and
-- src:9043 | (b) any obligation of the company to state in a statement of capital the rights attached to the shares extends to the terms, conditions and manner of redemption.
@ref s 685(3)(b) Any obligation to state in a statement of capital the rights attached to the shares extends to the terms, conditions and manner of redemption (src:9041-9043)
GIVEN `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is obliged to state in a statement of capital the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 685(3)(b) the obligation to state the rights extends to the terms, conditions and manner of redemption` MEANS
    IF `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)` AND `the company is obliged to state in a statement of capital the rights attached to the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors are authorised under subsection (1) ... any obligation of the company to state in a statement of capital the rights attached to the shares extends to the terms, conditions and manner of redemption"

-- src:9044 | (4) Where the directors are not so authorised, the terms, conditions and manner of redemption of any redeemable shares must be stated in the company's articles.
@ref s 685(4) Where the directors are not authorised, the terms must be stated in the company's articles (src:9044-9044)
GIVEN `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 685(4) the terms, conditions and manner of redemption must be stated in the company's articles` MEANS
    IF `the directors are authorised under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors are not so authorised"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 686: payment for redeemable shares ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9046 | (1) Redeemable shares in a limited company may not be redeemed unless they are fully paid.
@ref s 686(1) Redeemable shares may not be redeemed unless they are fully paid (src:9046-9046)
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 686(1) the redemption is barred` MEANS
    IF `the shares are fully paid`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be redeemed unless they are fully paid"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9047 | (2) The terms of redemption of shares in a limited company may provide that the amount payable on redemption may, by agreement between the company and the holder of the shares, be paid on a date later than the redemption date.
@ref s 686(2) The terms of redemption may provide that the amount payable on redemption is paid on a later date by agreement (src:9047-9047)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount payable on redemption is to be paid on a date later than the redemption date by agreement between the company and the holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 686(2) the terms of redemption may provide for payment on a later date` MEANS
    IF `the company is a limited company`
       AND `the amount payable on redemption is to be paid on a date later than the redemption date by agreement between the company and the holder of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The terms of redemption of shares in a limited company may provide that the amount payable on redemption may, by agreement between the company and the holder of the shares, be paid on a date later than the redemption date"

-- src:9048 | (3) Unless redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2), the shares must be paid for on redemption.
@ref s 686(3) Unless redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2), the shares must be paid for on redemption (src:9048-9048)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 686(3) the shares must be paid for on redemption` MEANS
    IF `the shares are redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 686(3) Unless redeemed in accordance with a provision authorised by subsection (2), the shares must be paid for on redemption (src:9048-9048)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 685(3) act in Chapter 3`
`s 686(3) the company must pay for the shares on redemption` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 686(3) pay for the shares on redemption`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 686(3): the shares were not paid for on redemption"

-- ---- s 687: financing of redemption ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9050 | (1) A private limited company may redeem redeemable shares out of capital in accordance with Chapter 5.
@ref s 687(1) A private limited company may redeem redeemable shares out of capital in accordance with Chapter 5 (src:9050-9050)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the redemption is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 687(1) the private limited company may redeem the shares out of capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private limited company may redeem redeemable shares out of capital"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the redemption is in accordance with Chapter 5`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with Chapter 5"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the redemption is in accordance with Chapter 5 is ss 709 to 723, answered by the caller

-- src:9051 | (2) Subject to that, redeemable shares in a limited company may only be redeemed out of—
-- src:9052 | (a) distributable profits of the company, or
-- src:9053 | (b) the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption.
@ref s 687(2) Subject to that, redeemable shares may only be redeemed out of distributable profits or the proceeds of a fresh issue (src:9051-9053)
GIVEN `s 687(1) the private limited company may redeem the shares out of capital` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the redemption is out of distributable profits of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the redemption is out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 687(2) the redemption is out of a source the section permits` MEANS
    IF (`s 687(1) the private limited company may redeem the shares out of capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR `the redemption is out of distributable profits of the company`
       OR `the redemption is out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 687(1) the private limited company may redeem the shares out of capital` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the redemption is out of capital under subsection (1) is not known, and the exception "Subject to that" turns on it
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "redeemable shares in a limited company may only be redeemed out of— (a) distributable profits of the company, or (b) the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption"

-- s 687(4): "whichever is the less". The proceeds of a fresh issue may meet the premium up to the lesser of (a) and (b).
-- src:9055 | (4) If the redeemable shares were issued at a premium, any premium payable on their redemption may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption, up to an amount equal to—
-- src:9056 | (a) the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares redeemed, or
-- src:9057 | (b) the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares),
-- src:9058 | whichever is the less.
@ref s 687(4) A premium on redemption may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue up to the lesser of the premiums received and the share premium account (src:9055-9058)
GIVEN `the redeemable shares were issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares redeemed` IS A NUMBER
      `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 687(4) the most of the premium that may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` MEANS
    IF `the redeemable shares were issued at a premium`
    THEN IF `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares redeemed` AT MOST `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)`
         THEN `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares redeemed`
         ELSE `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the redeemable shares were issued at a premium": no allowance otherwise

-- src:9054 | (3) Any premium payable on redemption of shares in a limited company must be paid out of distributable profits of the company, subject to the following provision.
@ref s 687(3) Any premium payable on redemption must be paid out of distributable profits, subject to subsection (4) (src:9054-9054)
GIVEN `the premium payable on redemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the most of the premium that subsection (4) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 687(3) the part of the premium that must be paid out of distributable profits` MEANS
    IF `the premium payable on redemption` AT MOST `the most of the premium that subsection (4) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the premium payable on redemption` MINUS `the most of the premium that subsection (4) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue`

-- src:9059 | (5) The amount of the company's share premium account is reduced by a sum corresponding (or by sums in the aggregate corresponding) to the amount of any payment made under subsection (4).
@ref s 687(5) The company's share premium account is reduced by a sum corresponding to any payment made under subsection (4) (src:9059-9059)
GIVEN `the amount of the company's share premium account before the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the payment made under subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 687(5) the amount of the company's share premium account after the payment` MEANS
    `the amount of the company's share premium account before the payment` MINUS `the payment made under subsection (4)`

-- src:9060 | (6) This section is subject to section 735(4) (terms of redemption enforceable in a winding up).
@ref s 687(6) This section is subject to section 735(4) (terms of redemption enforceable in a winding up) (src:9060-9060)
GIVEN `s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 687(6) the limits of section 687 on the source of payment are displaced by section 735(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- the section has effect subject to section 735(4): where the terms may be enforced in the winding up, section 687(2) does not stop the payment (fork F-signpost)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section is subject to section 735(4)": the text displaces the section only as section 735(4) enforces the terms, and says nothing of the case where it does not
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 735(4) lets the terms be enforced is not known

-- ---- s 688: redeemed shares treated as cancelled ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9062 | Where shares in a limited company are redeemed—
-- src:9063 | (a) the shares are treated as cancelled, and
@ref s 688(a) Where shares in a limited company are redeemed, the shares are treated as cancelled (src:9062-9063)
GIVEN `shares in a limited company are redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 688(a) the shares are treated as cancelled` MEANS
    IF `shares in a limited company are redeemed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares in a limited company are redeemed"

-- src:9062 | Where shares in a limited company are redeemed—
-- src:9063 | (a) the shares are treated as cancelled, and
-- src:9064 | (b) the amount of the company's issued share capital is diminished accordingly by the nominal value of the shares redeemed.
@ref s 688(b) Where shares in a limited company are redeemed, the issued share capital is diminished by the nominal value of the shares redeemed (src:9062-9064)
GIVEN `shares in a limited company are redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the redemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the shares redeemed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 688(b) the amount of the company's issued share capital after the redemption` MEANS
    IF `shares in a limited company are redeemed`
    THEN `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the redemption` MINUS `the nominal value of the shares redeemed`
    ELSE `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the redemption` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares in a limited company are redeemed": no diminution otherwise

-- ---- s 689: notice to registrar of redemption ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9066 | (1) If a limited company redeems any redeemable shares it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar, specifying the shares redeemed.
@ref s 689(1) A limited company that redeems redeemable shares must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar (src:9066-9066)
GIVEN `the date on which the company redeemed the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 689(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` MEANS `add months` `the date on which the company redeemed the shares` 1
-- fork F-month: "within one month" is read as the corresponding date one month on (clamped to the month's last day); the other reading ends on the day before it

@ref s 689(1) A limited company that redeems redeemable shares must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar (src:9066-9066)
GIVEN `the date on which the company redeemed the shares` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 689(1) the notice was given within one month after the redemption` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the company redeemed the shares`
       AND `the date on which the company gave notice to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 689(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date on which the company redeemed the shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar"

@ref s 689(1) A limited company that redeems redeemable shares must within one month after doing so give notice to the registrar (src:9066-9066)
GIVEN `the date on which the company redeemed the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 685(3) act in Chapter 3`
`s 689(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 689(1) give notice to the registrar of the redemption, specifying the shares redeemed`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 689(1) the last day for giving notice to the registrar` `the date on which the company redeemed the shares`) MINUS Day `the date on which the company redeemed the shares`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 689(1): notice of the redemption was not given to the registrar within one month after the redemption"

